# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This tree is 12 GB on disk and ~75 MB of it is source. Everything below is
# the other 11.9 GB: compiler and bundler output from four toolchains, all of
# it reproducible from what is tracked. Measured 2026-08-09:
#
#   spikes/strict-mode/build      2.9 GB      force-old/.build      3.5 GB
#   spikes/tauri-gate/…/target    1.6 GB      spikes/flutter-gate   1.6 GB
#
# The spikes are throwaway probes (see spikes/RESULTS.md). Their *source* is
# worth keeping — the answer each one produced is the point — but nothing in
# them needs to build from a clone.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Swift / Xcode
.build/
.swiftpm/
*.xcodeproj/
*.xcworkspace/
xcuserdata/
DerivedData/

# Flutter / Dart — spikes/flutter-gate, spikes/flutter-showcase, spikes/strict-mode
build/
.dart_tool/
.flutter-plugins
.flutter-plugins-dependencies
.packages
*.iml

# Rust / Tauri — spikes/tauri-gate
target/

# Node
node_modules/
.next/
.turbo/

# Android
.gradle/
local.properties
*.apk
*.aab

# CocoaPods
Pods/

# Distributable builds (may contain baked keys — see force-old/.gitignore)
dist/

# Secrets. force-old/web/.gitignore already covers its own .env*; this is the
# root-level backstop so a new subproject cannot leak one by not having a
# .gitignore of its own yet.
.env
.env.*
!.env*.example

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOT ignored, deliberately:
#
#   design/built/   6.6 MB of generated HTML. HANDOFF.md said this belongs
#                   here, and that was the right instinct for generated output
#                   — but these five pages ARE the design artifacts, they have
#                   been lost once already (rebuilt 2026-08-07 from Claude file
#                   history after every published URL 404'd), and 6.6 MB is a
#                   cheap insurance premium against losing them twice. The
#                   source in design/parts/ is tracked too, so build.py can
#                   still regenerate them.
#
# Note `build/` above does not match `design/built/` — different word.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
